alted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=338068#post338068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So naturally she resorts to a stripper outfit themed in a culture found, as far as we know, nowhere in Creation.<br /> <br /> This train of reasoning never even made it to the tracks.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not necessarily a Catholic habit. It could be the habit of a Buddhist nun, and Buddhism aesthetics appear all over Creation. Which isn't to say that worship of certain beings, i.e. that of UCS or Malfeas or Cecelyne, could not be very Catholic in nature in certain places; the imagery and pomp certainly fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T10:07:36-08:00","id":338130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=338074#post338074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P/s: The comic's flow will be better with 3 or 4 panels, but I'm way too lazy :cough:</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it works just fine.<br /> <br /> The second panel is amazing. The sense of motion with Cearr's completed back-hand swing, the corpse's boobs flopping back from the air-force, and Sulumor's feet alone conveying that she's doing a Luigi-esque Smash Brothers twirl as she flies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T10:38:00-08:00","id":338162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=338110#post338110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not necessarily a Catholic habit. It could be the habit of a Buddhist nun, and Buddhism aesthetics appear all over Creation. Which isn't to say that worship of certain beings, i.e. that of UCS or Malfeas or Cecelyne, could not be very Catholic in nature in certain places; the imagery and pomp certainly fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was said to be the garb of a Stavrophore, which is Eastern Orthodox. The criticism remains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T10:46:09-08:00","id":338169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=338162#post338162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was said to be the garb of a Stavrophore, which is Eastern Orthodox. The criticism remains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for my own clarification: your criticism is that some religions in Creation might have similar trappings, rituals, or aesthetics of real-world religions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T11:22:20-08:00","id":338205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=338169#post338169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for my own clarification: your criticism is that some religions in Creation might have similar trappings, rituals, or aesthetics of real-world religions?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's that Eastern Orthodox Christianity doesn't come up anywhere else in the setting as an aesthetic, so it's really silly to have a stripper outfit variant on a character because she &quot;lacks a reference frame.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 12-12-2014, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:56:52-08:00","id":338481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=337996#post337996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favouite version of her has a very simple answer to that question.<br /> She would never have chosen to be a Dune Person and spent most of her early life being quietly fascinated by the world beyond the dunes, kind of like The Little Mermaid if Ariel had cultural expectations to lure any humans she met to a watery grave. Also if Ariel's view of surface people wasn't so much &quot;we shouldn't kill them&quot; so much as &quot;why don't we kill them and take their stuff?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sulumor wishes to obtain peace from a position of strength.<br /> Its just that currently the Dune People are predators, feared but not respected its only a matter of time before someone gets their act together and plans a successful cull. As such the only way forward is to get organised before faced with the prospect of extinction because by then it would be too late.<br /> Some consider her extreme views a form of cultural extinction. To continue the Little Mermaid analogy she ran King Triton through because she knew that her father could never accept her vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"d