> <br /> (Am I the only one who thought that the Demjen, 1CD &quot;mermaids&quot; who swim through the air while singing, with their metallic crab friends, were a deliberate ref to TLM?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 12-13-2014, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T11:26:13-08:00","id":339237,"title":"","content":"Funny enough I just happened to saw that on imgur while also browsing the thread and immediately thought that'd fit as an Infernal Ariel. Or an Abyssal one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T13:07:09-08:00","id":339363,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, unless they've got a form of magic like the Water Aspect Anima, applause underwater has got to be pretty awkward...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T23:00:14-08:00","id":340546,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject of Sulumor...<br /> <br /> Two things I didn't like about her background: <br /> <br /> 1) She was rejected as a Shaman by the local spirit court because they could sense a darkness about her destiny. But isn't Exaltation impossible to predict? Didn't it have to be that way so that the Primordials couldn't preemptively strike at candidates for Exaltation? To say nothing of the fact that Infernal Exaltations are Outside of Fate to begin with...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2) The very first thing she does when she hatches is to instantly summon a Beauteous Wasp to fly her to safety. What? What happened to the Trials of Initiation into Sorcery? What happened to needing the proper tools and offerings to summon a demon, which is a process that takes quite a bit of time? Unless there's some Cecelynian charm I'm forgetting that enables one to instantly port demons to Creation, this is just plain weird...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T23:26:48-08:00","id":340554,"title":"","content":"1. Exaltation doesn't completely obscure a person's destiny. It loosens it, I think is a good word.<br /> <br /> 2. Twilights, Air Aspects, and Daybreaks can &quot;accidentally&quot; initiate, at least into the lowest circle. I'm not sure which caste Sulumor is, or which Infernal caste corresponds to Twilight, but if she's the right caste, maybe that's what she did as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T23:27:31-08:00","id":340555,"title":"","content":"It's Scroll of Exalts. I knew White Wolf's track record with canon NPCs and expected it to be more miss than hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T02:27:36-08:00","id":340670,"title":"","content":"Sulumor is a Malefactor, which is Infernal-Zenith. <br /> <br /> I think what happened with her is that the shit she went through prior to exaltation was enough to count as the initiation. It's pretty vague so you could easily flesh it out until you feel the events qualify to a satisfactory standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T13:28:36-08:00","id":341141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=338052#post338052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd never considered before how Manosque Cyan is about the only signature character who has the decency to have her appearances in comics actually work towards developing her character and goals as depicted in a focused character write-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true!<br /> <br /> Panther's appearances in the comics work towards developing his goal of punching people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T14:13:12-08:00","id":341210,"title":"","content":"Strength-of-Many seems to match as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:15:10-08:00","id":341261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=340546#post340546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on the subject of Sulumor...<br /> <br /> Two things I didn't like about her background:<br /> <br /> 1) She was rejected as a Shaman by the local spirit court because they could sense a darkness about her destiny. But isn't Exaltation impossible to predict? Didn't it have to be that way so that the Primordials couldn't preemptively strike at candidates for Exaltation? To say nothing of the fact that Infernal Exaltations are Outside of Fate to begin with...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2) The very first thing she does when she hatches is to instantly summon a Beauteous Wasp to fly her to safety. What? What happened to the Trials of Initiation into Sorcery? What happened to needing the proper tools and offerings to summon a demon, which is a process that takes quite a bit of time? Unless there's some Cecelynian charm I'm forgetting that enables one to instantly port demons to Creation, this is just plain weird...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to impose crunch standards on narrative is pretty much never a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:36:58-08:00","id":341270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength-of-Many seems to match as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Strneght-of-Many is that guy who fights slavers and frees slaves, so every single comic has him bellowing about how terrible slavers are before doing something terrible to one; he falls under my standard of &quot;around in a manner vaguely illustrative of their character stereotype&quot;. Cyan's comics actually follow a continuous thread of action, each one building off of something established in another. Indeed, she actually ties up a few thread established in prior comics (or at least one of them, building on that Poramo/Nagezzer meeting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:49:32-08:00","id":341285,"title":"","content":"He gets a bit of development in the one where he lets two guys he just freed follow him around for a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T20:15:42-08:00","id":341490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341270#post341270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Strneght-of-Many is that guy who fights slavers and frees slaves, so every single comic has him bellowing about how terrible slavers are before doing something terrible to one; he falls under my standard of &quot;around in a manner vaguely illustrative of their character stereotype&quot;. Cyan's comics actually follow a continuous thread of action, each one building off of something established in another. Indeed, she actually ties up a few thread established in prior comics (or at least one of them, building on that Poramo/Nagezzer meeting).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do wonder whether she survive in that RotSE comic where she is about to be gank from behind by Nagezzer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 12-15-2014, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T20:28:40-08:00","id":341498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341285#post341285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He gets a bit of development in the one where he lets two guys he just freed follow him around for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love that one<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341490#post341490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder whether she survive in that RotSE comic where she is about to be gank from behind by Nagezzer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Been wondering that too. That was actually the first comic I read with her, and I thought &quot;woops. well, She's probably a goner&quot;.<br /> Later I found out who/what her character actually was...<br /> I'm guessing Nagezzer will try for an attack to kill a mortal, assuming that she is simply a spy for another house (as I assumed when reading the comic, and not knowing anything about 2ed) which probably will make her end up less dead than he'd imagined.<br /> ... aaaaand I'm guessing that if you don't kill her before she's aware of your intent, you might be in... &quot;trouble&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T21:35:08-08:00","id":341536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=340554#post340554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Exaltation doesn't completely obscure a person's destiny. It loosens it, I think is a good word.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if true, it still doesn't really work. In Exalted, there is no &quot;seeing into the future&quot;, for realzies. The charms that seem to do so operate by reading *the plans written up for the future in the Loom of Fate*...the spirit charm version, which is what would be used here, explicitly works that way. Sulumor's future should have read &quot;clear skies ahead&quot; or whatever the B of D had in store for her, and any type of Exaltation (beyond 'sidereal and DB that is) would not show up in it, even if she does Exalt as some sort of Celestial later on. <br /> <br /> Granted, all of this is subject to change in the new edition, but that's my understanding of how things work now. <br /> <br /> Anyway, her origin story doesn't bug me nearly as much as Cyan's! Don't even get me started...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T21:41:59-08:00","id":341541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=338052#post338052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd never considered before how Manosque Cyan is about the only signature character who has the decency to have her appearances in comics actually work towards developing her character and goals as depicted in a focused character write-up. It's like &quot;hey, we'll write this character as having a beef against the Realm and also happily getting one over on its powerful folks as she works within its system to bring it down, <i>and then actually show her doing that stuff in the comics</i>&quot;. There's even a kind of little arc to it. Can you name me any other character who has something like that, rather than, at best, just dicking around in a manner vaguely illustrative of their character stereotype?</div> </div> </div> </div>Drogath?<br /> <br /> We see him exalt as an obnoxious brat while beating the school teacher who dared to attempt to discipline him, and get to see that he doesn't become much less arrogant as an adult in the Exalted comic book miniseries. After that, he pops up now and then in various chapter comics. Unfortunately, we don't get to SEE much of his character growth, but it's clear by his final appearance in RotSE, where he's sacrificed his life to summon the Five Metal Shrike to take out the Realm's troops and Arjuna, that he has become quite a different man...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T21:55:27-08:00","id":341557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341261#post341261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to impose crunch standards on narrative is pretty much never a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I suppose a freshly Exalted Solar should pull off an Essence 5 Melee Charm despite previously having no Melee rating at all? Just because it was cool and was an easy way for the author to write the character out of the situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-16-2014, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T02:01:52-08:00","id":341653,"title":"","content":"I think an initial burst of power beyond what they could normally do is a workable quirk of exaltation. You get a sudden surge as the power hits, pull an unbelievable move out of your ass and when it's over you're standing there going &quot;Now how the fuck did I do that?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T02:12:56-08:00","id":341654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drogath?</div> </div> </div> </div> I find that to be more of a cute little call back than anything. Note that when I say &quot;development&quot;, I don't really mean &quot;wow, that Cyan is really growing as a person/we are given more insights into her&quot;, I'm just talking about how each comic is a step in a connected narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T02:15:58-08:00","id":341656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=340546#post340546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on the subject of Sulumor...<br /> <br /> Two things I didn't like about her background:<br /> <br /> 1) She was rejected as a Shaman by the local spirit court because they could sense a darkness about her destiny. But isn't Exaltation impossible to predict? Didn't it have to be that way so that the Primordials couldn't preemptively strike at candidates for Exaltation? To say nothing of the fact that Infernal Exaltations are Outside of Fate to begin with...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2) The very first thing she does when she hatches is to instantly summon a Beauteous Wasp to fly her to safety. What? What happened to the Trials of Initiation into Sorcery? What happened to needing the proper tools and offerings to summon a demon, which is a process that takes quite a bit of time? Unless there's some Cecelynian charm I'm forgetting that enables one to instantly port demons to Creation, this is just plain weird...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Who says she was destined to become an Infernal? There are other dark destinies in the world, and it may be that the Yozis inadvertently prevented her from fulfilling a very dark destiny indeed...<br /> <br /> 2) If there IS a Charm to instantly summon demons, Cecylene is a pretty good place to put it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T02:17:12-08:00","id":341657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=337959#post337959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that way she at least feels a bit related to the Exalted world instead of just being a hellnun?<br /> Seriously, Sulumor does not feel like she's part of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed. The entire concept of the sexualized nun to represent the infernal is so out of place in Creation that it's hard to fathom how it made it through to the book. The idea it implies of sexuality and female dominant sexuality in particular as moral-depravity of the sacred is grossly out of place in Creation's cultures. I mean there are celibate groups like the Immaculate Order - but that's about personal detachment from fleshy concerns - a sexualized Immaculate would be seen in the Realm as personally weak, not spiritually/morally threatening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T02:19:59-08:00","id":341659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341261#post341261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to impose crunch standards on narrative is pretty much never a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The narrative requirements of Sorcery are setting principles not a loose mechanical emulation there-of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T04:05:10-08:00","id":341732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341657#post341657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. The entire concept of the sexualized nun to represent the infernal is so out of place in Creation that it's hard to fathom how it made it through to the book. The idea it implies of sexuality and female dominant sexuality in particular as moral-depravity of the sacred is grossly out of place in Creation's cultures. I mean there are celibate groups like the Immaculate Order - but that's about personal detachment from fleshy concerns - a sexualized Immaculate would be seen in the Realm as personally weak, not spiritually/morally threatening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to remember it being said of Thousand Faceted Nelumbo that they were basically given artwork and told to figure out a backstory. I wouldn't have been shocked if this happened with the Infernals too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T04:12:40-08:00","id":341733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341656#post341656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Who says she was destined to become an Infernal? There are other dark destinies in the world, and it may be that the Yozis inadvertently prevented her from fulfilling a very dark destiny indeed...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Jugo could sensed what she would do with any power, or simply have just taken a dislike to the ambitious young woman and made the claim as an excuse to exile her; <i>ironically</i> banishing her to an actual &quot;dark destiny&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341656#post341656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) If there IS a Charm to instantly summon demons, Cecylene is a pretty good place to put it...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Emerald Circle Infernal spell. Sulumor's &quot;Slave Spawn Summons&quot; spell summons, and binds. first circle demons at sunset <i>without</i> the extensive ritual time of &quot;Demon of the First Circle&quot;. ( MoEP:Infernals 165, Scroll of Exalts 139 )<br /> <br /> However, using the Sorcerous Enlightenment of (Yozi) charm to still requires the Green Sun Princes to undergo the five quests to initiate. She shouldn't have been able to 'instinctively' use sorcery immediately after transformation. But whatever; handwave it for the sake of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T04:24:43-08:00","id":341737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341657#post341657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean there are celibate groups like the Immaculate Order - but that's about personal detachment from fleshy concerns - a sexualized Immaculate would be seen in the Realm as personally weak, not spiritually/morally threatening.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good. I am going to paraphrase it a lot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T09:43:53-08:00","id":342024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341653#post341653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an initial burst of power beyond what they could normally do is a workable quirk of exaltation. You get a sudden surge as the power hits, pull an unbelievable move out of your ass and when it's over you're standing there going &quot;Now how the fuck did I do that?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. That actually is one of my favored ideas.<br /> <br /> But if so, it had better be possible to summon a demon through Endless Desert Charms, because Sorcery shouldn't be one of those &quot;first surge&quot; possibilities.<br /> <br /> And ideally, neither should Charms for which you have no score at all, as in the example. If a second-breathing Solar needs to get out of trouble, maybe he's not good at swords because he's better at running away.<br /> <br /> But the new Exalt's general aptitudes should be suited for surviving the situation, or else circumstances should intervene to save them. Because not all Celestial Exalted are supposed to survive their Second Breaths -- just the ones who go on to become NPCs and player characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:46:26-08:00","id":342346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=341733#post341733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the Emerald Circle Infernal spell. Sulumor's &quot;Slave Spawn Summons&quot; spell summons, and binds. first circle demons at sunset <i>without</i> the extensive ritual time of &quot;Demon of the First Circle&quot;. ( MoEP:Infernals 165, Scroll of Exalts 139 )<br /> <br /> However, using the Sorcerous Enlightenment of (Yozi) charm to still requires the Green Sun Princes to undergo the five quests to initiate. She shouldn't have been able to 'instinctively' use sorcery immediately after transformation. But whatever; handwave it for the sake of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly using this as a launching point. I don't think it's as implausible as people are maintaining, even knowing next to nothing about Sulumor than details mentioned in this thread.<br /> <br /> Aside from the fifth, the Stations of Sorcery don't have to be things the individual consciously seeks at the time, simply wisdom and/or experiences they have come to possess.* One technically needs to be Enlightened, but actively being remolded into a Green Sun Prince within a Chrysalis Grotesque (or even in the moment of accepting the demon's offer...?) feels close enough to me. Sulumor letting go of some idea that was rather significant to her (possibly that things could one day be the same again?) would be a way for her to initiate into Sorcery.<br /> <br /> * I believe <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0284.html\" target=\"_blank\">Keychain of Creation</a> presented the Trials correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T18:23:32-08:00","id":342452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=342346#post342346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the fifth, the Stations of Sorcery don't have to be things the individual consciously seeks at the time, simply wisdom and/or experiences they have come to possess.* One technically needs to be Enlightened, but actively being remolded into a Green Sun Prince within a Chrysalis Grotesque (or even in the moment of accepting the demon's offer...?) feels close enough to me. Sulumor letting go of some idea that was rather significant to her (possibly that things could one day be the same again?) would be a way for her to initiate into Sorcery.<br /> <br /> * I believe <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0284.html\" target=\"_blank\">Keychain of Creation</a> presented the Trials correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. The Five Ordeals are of Humility, Tutelage, Journey, Fear, and Sacrifice. Sulumor's backstory does sort of cover each station; or at least they could be slipped into it as she was <i>studying</i> to be a shaman before being <i>exiled</i> to die of exposure. So I guess the initiation as part and parcel of the transfiguration is somewhat plausible.<br /> <br /> Still, that leaves the part is about the casting of a spell by 'instinct', and immediately after emerging. As Keychain of Creation indicates, <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0283.html\" target=\"_blank\">casting sorcery isn't an instinctive process</a>. It doesn't fit the narrative about sorcery at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 12-16-2014, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T20:04:18-08:00","id":342540,"title":"","content":"Actually... Sorcery isn't instinctive for *most* Exalts. Green Sun Princes use essence the same way as the Primordials, and for the Primordials, Sorcery IS natural; hence the Sorcerious keyword; a number of Infernal Charms effectively ARE Sorcery!<br /> <br /> Infernals aren't just Solars with a coat of green paint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:30:49-08:00","id":342590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=342540#post342540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually... Sorcery isn't instinctive for *most* Exalts. Green Sun Princes use essence the same way as the Primordials, and for the Primordials, Sorcery IS natural; hence the Sorcerious keyword; a number of Infernal Charms effectively ARE Sorcery!</div> </div> </div> </div>Some infernal charms have <i>sorcerous effects</i>; in that they can be countered or dispelled as if such, and are maintained independently (enduring without essence commitment, but also can't be dispersed at will), and so on.<br /> <br /> This does <i><b>not</b> </i>mean actual spells are <i>learned and used </i>like charms by an Infernal exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T22:41:14-08:00","id":342643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337752-could-a-dune-person-exalt-as-a-sidereal?p=342590#post342590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some infernal charms have <i>sorcerous effects</i>; in that they can be countered or dispelled as if such, and are maintained independently (enduring without essence commitment, but also can't be dispersed at will), and so on.<br /> <br /> This does <i><b>not</b> </i>mean actual spells are <i>learned and used </i>like charms by an Infernal exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Other way around... Infernal Charms are learned and used like spells. Not one of them is just a natural extension of skill - every single one of them is hard work forcing your essence patterns into alien geometry. So learning a spell during the transformation is roughly the same as learning a Charm during it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}